<Hub pillarId="trending-explained">
  <p>
    A headline is a bad teacher. It is short on purpose, and the short version is where the hype hides.
  </p>
  <p>
    This topic is for news that beginners are actually asking about: a new rule, a scam warning, a word that suddenly shows up in group chats. We will explain it only after we can link a primary source. A regulator page, a statute, an official project document, or a paper. A social post is not enough on its own. Our <a href="/sourcing/">sourcing rules</a> say so.
  </p>
  <p>
    We will not publish a price target, a “what to buy this week” list, or a recap that repeats a press release without adding a plain-English explanation. If two official sources disagree, the guide will say that they disagree.
  </p>
  <p>
    Until a news guide clears that bar, use the path that is already done. <a href="/articles/what-is-bitcoin/">What bitcoin is</a>. <a href="/articles/crypto-scams-to-avoid/">Which messages to ignore</a>. <a href="/editorial-policy/">What we refuse to publish</a>.
  </p>
</Hub>
